abstract: >-
  This repository is the open-source artifact for the paper
  "Equipment Thickness Theory: A Formal Model for Agent Capability Stacks"
  (ICLR 2027 Main submission, 2026-09-25). It contributes (1) a SkillDAG
  of 207 agent skills connected by 159 typed edges in 6 categories, used
  to measure the structural complexity of multi-agent systems; (2) an
  Action Policy Check module implementing 10 rules across 5 categories
  with 3 decision levels (allow / ask / deny); (3) a Model Router
  supporting 4 LLM providers across 10 task categories with a 5-rule
  cost-aware selection policy and a 20-field audit log; (4) a Semantic
  Recall module indexing 361 memory chunks under 3 query modes (keyword,
  semantic, hybrid); and (5) a 35-case weekly evaluation harness
  spanning 7 categories. Reproducing the full sweep takes approximately
  30 seconds on a single MacBook Air with no GPU. The artifact
  accompanies the double-blind submission; author names and a permanent
  Zenodo DOI will be added at acceptance. The companion workshop paper
  ("Misevolution in Practice: A 2-Month Empirical Study") shares these
  artifacts and adds a 25-item MLAS checklist runner with 20 test cases.